1
00:00:02,777 --> 00:00:03,378
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, yeah.

2
00:00:03,518 --> 00:00:16,811
[SPEAKER_00]: So, today's sutta is Madhyamanikaya 62, which is the longer advice to Venerable Rahula.

3
00:00:17,252 --> 00:00:21,937
[SPEAKER_00]: At one time, the Buddha was staying near Savatthi in Jetha's grove, Anathapindika's monastery.

4
00:00:23,382 --> 00:00:28,191
[SPEAKER_00]: When the Buddha robed up in the morning, taking his ball and robe, he entered Savatthi for alms.

5
00:00:28,511 --> 00:00:32,980
[SPEAKER_00]: There he met Venerable Rahula, who also robed up and followed behind him.

6
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:51,164
[SPEAKER_00]: The Buddha looked back and said, Rahula, you should see any kind of form at all, past, future or present, internal, external, coarse or fine, inferior or superior, far or near, all form as it actually is, with right understanding.

7
00:00:51,865 --> 00:00:52,765
[SPEAKER_00]: This is not mine.

8
00:00:53,086 --> 00:00:53,906
[SPEAKER_00]: I am not this.

9
00:00:54,327 --> 00:00:55,568
[SPEAKER_00]: This is not myself.

10
00:00:57,629 --> 00:01:01,733
[SPEAKER_00]: Rahula asked in return, only form, auspicious one, only form?

11
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:06,562
[SPEAKER_00]: Form, as well as feeling, is perception, activities and consciousness.

12
00:01:06,742 --> 00:01:08,303
[SPEAKER_00]: In other words, the five aggregates.

13
00:01:08,363 --> 00:01:16,567
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the five aggregates should be seen as this is not mine, I am not this and this is not myself.

14
00:01:17,328 --> 00:01:24,651
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then the Venerable Rākula thought, well, who would go to the village for alms today after being advised directly by the Buddha?

15
00:01:25,232 --> 00:01:31,315
[SPEAKER_00]: Turning back, he sat down cross-legged at the root of a certain tree, setting his body straight, establishing recollection at the fore.

16
00:01:33,227 --> 00:01:35,609
[SPEAKER_00]: Venerable Sariputta saw him there and addressed him.

17
00:01:35,809 --> 00:01:37,870
[SPEAKER_00]: Rāhula developed the recollection of breathing.

18
00:01:38,090 --> 00:01:42,252
[SPEAKER_00]: When recollection of breathing is developed and cultivated, it's very fruitful and very beneficial.

19
00:01:43,753 --> 00:01:53,778
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, later in the afternoon, Rāhula went out for retreat, went to the Buddha and asked him, Venerable Sir, how is the recollection of the breathing developed and cultivated, so that it's fruitful and beneficial?

20
00:01:55,769 --> 00:02:23,172
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, the Buddha begins the longer instruction saying, anything internal pertaining to oneself that is hard, solid, appropriated, this includes head of the hair, body hair, nails, teeth, skin, flesh, sinews, bones, bone marrow, kidneys, heart, liver, diaphragm, spleen, lungs, intestines, mesentery, undigested food, feces or anything else internal pertaining to oneself that's hard, solid and appropriated.

21
00:02:23,967 --> 00:02:25,988
[SPEAKER_00]: This is called the internal earth element.

22
00:02:26,749 --> 00:02:31,372
[SPEAKER_00]: Both the internal earth element and the external earth element are just the earth element.

23
00:02:32,252 --> 00:02:34,714
[SPEAKER_00]: This should be seen as it is with right understanding.

24
00:02:34,754 --> 00:02:35,615
[SPEAKER_00]: This is not mine.

25
00:02:35,995 --> 00:02:36,535
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm not this.

26
00:02:36,835 --> 00:02:37,856
[SPEAKER_00]: This is not myself.

27
00:02:39,517 --> 00:02:42,799
[SPEAKER_00]: Having seen it with right understanding, one grows disenchanted with the earth element.

28
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:46,021
[SPEAKER_00]: One reads the mind of the passion for the earth element.

29
00:02:47,142 --> 00:02:48,923
[SPEAKER_00]: Then goes to describe the water element.

30
00:02:49,023 --> 00:02:49,244
[SPEAKER_00]: So,

31
00:02:50,967 --> 00:02:52,688
[SPEAKER_00]: Water element may be internal or external.

32
00:02:52,908 --> 00:02:54,269
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the internal water element?

33
00:02:54,490 --> 00:02:59,234
[SPEAKER_00]: Anything internal, pertaining to oneself, that's watery and appropriated.

34
00:02:59,954 --> 00:03:10,684
[SPEAKER_00]: This includes bile, phlegm, pus, blood, sweat, fat, tears, grease, saliva, snot, synovial fluid, urine, anything else internal, pertaining to oneself, that's water, watery or appropriated.

35
00:03:11,324 --> 00:03:12,746
[SPEAKER_00]: This is called the internal water element.

36
00:03:14,487 --> 00:03:18,632
[SPEAKER_00]: Both internal and external water element are the water, just the water element.

37
00:03:19,293 --> 00:03:24,679
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this should be seen with right understanding, like, this is not mine, I'm not this, this is not myself, and so on.

38
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:33,269
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the fire element, the fire element, internally, it's anything that's fire, fiery, warm, hot, appropriated, obviously.

39
00:03:34,270 --> 00:03:46,283
[SPEAKER_00]: This includes the warmth, that which warms, that which ages, that which heats you up when feverish, that which properly digests food and drink, anything else internal pertaining to oneself that's fire-fiery or appropriated... inappropriate.

40
00:03:47,175 --> 00:03:48,776
[SPEAKER_00]: This is called the internal fire element.

41
00:03:48,876 --> 00:03:51,057
[SPEAKER_00]: Both internal and external fire elements there.

42
00:03:51,257 --> 00:03:51,478
[SPEAKER_00]: Same.

43
00:03:52,138 --> 00:03:59,863
[SPEAKER_00]: Needs to be seen as this is not mine, that's not myself, I'm not this and that's not myself, in order for mine to be rid of the passion for the fire element.

44
00:04:00,823 --> 00:04:06,607
[SPEAKER_00]: And then the air element goes that anything airy, pertaining to oneself,

45
00:04:07,650 --> 00:04:18,256
[SPEAKER_00]: So, winds that go up and down, winds in the belly, of the bowels, winds that flow through the limbs, in-breath, out-breath, anything else internal pertaining to oneself that's air, airy, or... and appropriated.

46
00:04:18,456 --> 00:04:20,137
[SPEAKER_00]: This is called the eternal air element.

47
00:04:20,277 --> 00:04:24,440
[SPEAKER_00]: Both internal and external means the air element is there.

48
00:04:26,201 --> 00:04:28,142
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this also needs to be seen as this is not mine.

49
00:04:28,362 --> 00:04:28,862
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm not this.

50
00:04:28,942 --> 00:04:29,883
[SPEAKER_00]: This is not myself.

51
00:04:31,393 --> 00:04:34,615
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the space element is added here for practical reasons.

52
00:04:34,895 --> 00:04:36,076
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll explain that later.

53
00:04:37,096 --> 00:04:39,597
[SPEAKER_00]: So, any space element that may be internal or external.

54
00:04:39,838 --> 00:04:41,118
[SPEAKER_00]: What is internal space element?

55
00:04:41,338 --> 00:04:45,240
[SPEAKER_00]: Anything internal and pertaining to oneself that is space, spacious and appropriated.

56
00:04:45,901 --> 00:04:57,107
[SPEAKER_00]: Includes ear canals, nostrils, mouth, space for swallowing what is eaten and drunk, space where it stays, space for excreting it from the nether regions, or anything else internal pertaining to oneself that's space, spacious and appropriated.

57
00:04:57,987 --> 00:05:04,993
[SPEAKER_00]: This is called the internal space element and both internal space element and the external space element means the space element is just there.

58
00:05:06,053 --> 00:05:07,435
[SPEAKER_00]: This should be seen with right understanding.

59
00:05:07,495 --> 00:05:08,215
[SPEAKER_00]: This is not mine.

60
00:05:08,335 --> 00:05:08,936
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm not this.

61
00:05:09,036 --> 00:05:10,157
[SPEAKER_00]: This is not myself.

62
00:05:10,537 --> 00:05:14,160
[SPEAKER_00]: Having seen it with right understanding, he grows disenchanted with the space element.

63
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:16,962
[SPEAKER_00]: He reads the mind of passion for the space element.

64
00:05:18,616 --> 00:05:25,461
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then the Buddha gives him a bit of a more, kind of, even more practical context to develop.

65
00:05:26,222 --> 00:05:28,023
[SPEAKER_00]: Says, develop your mind like Earth.

66
00:05:29,044 --> 00:05:33,727
[SPEAKER_00]: Or, your mind is added here, obviously, for the sake of clarity, but just says, develop yourself like Earth.

67
00:05:33,847 --> 00:05:34,868
[SPEAKER_00]: Just develop like Earth.

68
00:05:35,909 --> 00:05:41,133
[SPEAKER_00]: When you develop like Earth, a reason agreeable and disagreeable pressures will not occupy your mind.

69
00:05:42,015 --> 00:05:46,719
[SPEAKER_00]: Suppose they were to toss both clean and unclean things on the earth, like feces, urine, spit, pus and blood.

70
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:50,283
[SPEAKER_00]: The earth isn't horrified, repelled or disgusted because of this.

71
00:05:51,003 --> 00:05:54,226
[SPEAKER_00]: In the same way, develop like earth.

72
00:05:54,707 --> 00:06:00,172
[SPEAKER_00]: For when you develop like earth, unreasonable, agreeable and disagreeable pressures will not endure with a grip on your mind.

73
00:06:01,888 --> 00:06:07,492
[SPEAKER_00]: Develop like water, for when you develop like water, a reason agreeable and disagreeable pressure will not occupy your mind.

74
00:06:07,812 --> 00:06:13,236
[SPEAKER_00]: Suppose there were to wash both clean and unclean things in the water, like feces, urine, spit, pus and blood.

75
00:06:14,036 --> 00:06:17,478
[SPEAKER_00]: The water isn't horrified, repelled, disgusted because of this.

76
00:06:18,279 --> 00:06:21,281
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in the same way, develop like water.

77
00:06:21,321 --> 00:06:28,886
[SPEAKER_00]: When you develop like water, a reason agreeable and disagreeable pressures will not... will not endure with a grip on your mind.

78
00:06:30,207 --> 00:06:43,915
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, develop like fire, kind of in the same way, so that there isn't an agreeable, disagreeable pressures do not occupy your mind, because the fire burns both clean and unclean things, and the fire isn't horrified, repelled and disgusted because of any of that.

79
00:06:45,517 --> 00:06:53,662
[SPEAKER_00]: Develop your mind like air, because the wind blows on both clean and unclean things, like feces, urine, spit, pus, and blood, and the wind isn't horrified, repelled.

80
00:06:53,703 --> 00:06:54,703
[SPEAKER_00]: Basically, it's indifferent.

81
00:06:55,444 --> 00:07:05,190
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in the same way, you should develop like earth, water, fire, air, so that arisen agreeable and disagreeable pressures.

82
00:07:05,290 --> 00:07:07,732
[SPEAKER_00]: Passa, common translations, contact.

83
00:07:08,492 --> 00:07:11,233
[SPEAKER_00]: will not endure with a grip on your mind.

84
00:07:11,693 --> 00:07:15,695
[SPEAKER_00]: So, basically, your mind will be above above that which is pressuring it.

85
00:07:17,335 --> 00:07:19,696
[SPEAKER_00]: And the last, it's develop your like space.

86
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:23,837
[SPEAKER_00]: For when develop like space, a reason agreeable, disagreeable pressures won't occupy your mind.

87
00:07:24,578 --> 00:07:34,281
[SPEAKER_00]: Just as a space is not established anywhere, in the same way, develop like space, so don't be established anywhere.

88
00:07:34,561 --> 00:07:35,982
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, it goes into develop friendliness.

89
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:38,601
[SPEAKER_00]: So that any ill will will be abandoned.

90
00:07:39,022 --> 00:07:41,964
[SPEAKER_00]: Develop compassion, so that any annoyance will be abandoned.

91
00:07:42,404 --> 00:07:45,747
[SPEAKER_00]: Develop contentment, so that any discontent will be abandoned.

92
00:07:45,907 --> 00:07:51,671
[SPEAKER_00]: Develop equanimity, so that any resistance, patīgā, will be abandoned.

93
00:07:51,811 --> 00:07:53,232
[SPEAKER_00]: Develop perception of non-beauty.

94
00:07:53,993 --> 00:07:55,674
[SPEAKER_00]: Develop the perception of impermanence.

95
00:07:56,134 --> 00:08:00,918
[SPEAKER_00]: And then it goes, in the end, develop the recollection of breathing, you know, that the whole question started with.

96
00:08:04,303 --> 00:08:08,185
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, before we go to the recollection of breathing, let's just quickly address these.

97
00:08:08,585 --> 00:08:09,505
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, maybe not so quickly.

98
00:08:10,266 --> 00:08:13,487
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the whole element contemplation.

99
00:08:15,208 --> 00:08:26,993
[SPEAKER_00]: Obviously, you know, people can start abstractly, in a sense of thinking about solid, hard things that are earth, that are made of stone and so on, just to get the idea.

100
00:08:27,033 --> 00:08:31,855
[SPEAKER_00]: But the point is to discern that internal earth element.

101
00:08:34,837 --> 00:08:45,667
[SPEAKER_00]: That which is usually overlooked, that which is usually not seen, that which is usually peripheral, that which is usually assumed and taken for granted and appropriated, as every passage here says.

102
00:08:46,467 --> 00:08:55,115
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the point is not to observe or monitor or attend to with your senses, to earth, water, fire, air.

103
00:08:55,135 --> 00:08:55,755
[SPEAKER_00]: The point is to

104
00:08:56,836 --> 00:09:05,005
[SPEAKER_00]: Include, basically, things, just broad things in your experience, that you generally overlook, because your attention is too absorbed with this thing or the other.

105
00:09:06,407 --> 00:09:14,296
[SPEAKER_00]: Include those peripheral things, so to see them as partaking in the same nature as this obvious earth around you.

106
00:09:14,756 --> 00:09:17,519
[SPEAKER_00]: Obvious fire, air, water, and so on.

107
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:28,706
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why in other suttas, when the Buddha talked about the elements, the element contemplation, it always kind of starts by, well, look at these these great mountains and see how they erode and get destroyed.

108
00:09:29,226 --> 00:09:33,408
[SPEAKER_00]: What is to be said of this little, kind of insignificant, weak, soft body?

109
00:09:34,789 --> 00:09:51,507
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the point is, you could try and kind of induce these feelings of like, okay, my body will change because the great earth element changed, because the great water element changed, but in order for that to not be abstract,

110
00:09:53,362 --> 00:10:07,046
[SPEAKER_00]: There needs to be something in your experience as a whole that you now recognize, that you now see as that internal earth element, that internal solid, that internal aspect of the airy, watery, fiery space.

111
00:10:08,066 --> 00:10:08,586
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's what I mean.

112
00:10:08,606 --> 00:10:13,948
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, it's not about discerning it through your direct attention.

113
00:10:14,769 --> 00:10:15,671
[SPEAKER_00]: and figuring it out.

114
00:10:16,373 --> 00:10:18,739
[SPEAKER_00]: It's about getting used to that which is already there.

115
00:10:18,779 --> 00:10:23,971
[SPEAKER_00]: So, instead of trying to attend to your body directly, to see hair, nails, teeth,

116
00:10:25,113 --> 00:10:28,015
[SPEAKER_00]: See it at the back of your mind, without needing to attend to it directly.

117
00:10:28,055 --> 00:10:32,639
[SPEAKER_00]: But know that there is hair, nails, teeth, flesh, sinews and bones.

118
00:10:32,719 --> 00:10:33,900
[SPEAKER_00]: They has to be there.

119
00:10:34,441 --> 00:10:37,923
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that peripheral knowledge that's not directly attended...

120
00:10:37,943 --> 00:10:46,110
[SPEAKER_00]: So, basically, you have to refrain from your tendency, from the desire to directly attend it and dissect it, because it will be object of your senses.

121
00:10:47,865 --> 00:10:53,006
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't want to see the body on the level of the object of your senses, which is sight, sound, smell, taste, sensations.

122
00:10:53,846 --> 00:10:56,847
[SPEAKER_00]: You want to see the body on the level of the sense bases.

123
00:10:57,047 --> 00:11:04,009
[SPEAKER_00]: You want to see the internal body, the one that's appropriate, the one that doesn't directly appear, the one that's always overlooked.

124
00:11:04,529 --> 00:11:05,589
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's where the problem is.

125
00:11:07,069 --> 00:11:10,190
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the whole practice of the four elements, it's not about

126
00:11:11,854 --> 00:11:22,487
[SPEAKER_00]: Memorizing all these things that the Buddha listed are solid and earthy and watery and fiery, it's more like discerning any of those aspects.

127
00:11:23,148 --> 00:11:26,192
[SPEAKER_00]: And sure, even if you think in those specific terms, that's fine, obviously.

128
00:11:26,893 --> 00:11:29,055
[SPEAKER_00]: But you need to think of them peripherally.

129
00:11:29,376 --> 00:11:30,918
[SPEAKER_00]: You need to be seeing them peripherally.

130
00:11:31,915 --> 00:11:43,550
[SPEAKER_00]: It needs to start to pertain to the knowledge of what's already there, as opposed to, oh, things are only there when I look at them directly, the moment my attention lapses, I forget about them.

131
00:11:44,491 --> 00:11:48,596
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's... that's not... well, pretty much, no contemplation works like that.

132
00:11:49,297 --> 00:12:05,001
[SPEAKER_00]: So, so the point of the four great element contemplation is to always have a reference point of your background, of that peripheral thing that endures, that shares the same nature like things that you do access with your senses directly, sight, sound, smell, taste, sensations.

133
00:12:07,201 --> 00:12:11,622
[SPEAKER_00]: And when you look at those things that are obviously changing,

134
00:12:12,679 --> 00:12:18,426
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't need to convince yourself that, okay, so now, because of that, my internal body will also change.

135
00:12:18,507 --> 00:12:18,647
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

136
00:12:19,147 --> 00:12:24,414
[SPEAKER_00]: By seeing it sufficiently enough that it's the same thing, as in, shares the same nature,

137
00:12:25,345 --> 00:12:34,453
[SPEAKER_00]: As it says, both internal or external, doesn't matter what kind of specific differences would have been perceived and evolved.

138
00:12:35,053 --> 00:12:42,499
[SPEAKER_00]: Fundamentally, anything pertaining to internal, anything pertaining to external that you can observe, means the earth element is just there.

139
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:46,362
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what you want to teach your mind.

140
00:12:46,442 --> 00:12:47,783
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what you want to sink in.

141
00:12:48,284 --> 00:12:51,426
[SPEAKER_00]: You want to know that anything internal

142
00:12:52,307 --> 00:12:56,768
[SPEAKER_00]: As I said, it doesn't matter like vague, clear, big or small, past, future.

143
00:12:57,969 --> 00:13:00,970
[SPEAKER_00]: Anything internal, anything external, shares the same nature.

144
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:10,613
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, when the obvious nature of external things is seen or you get reminded of, the internal counterpart cannot not be affected by it.

145
00:13:11,910 --> 00:13:12,371
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what I mean.

146
00:13:12,391 --> 00:13:18,518
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why I said, like, you won't have to convince yourself, then, that this internal is also like that external.

147
00:13:18,618 --> 00:13:19,659
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it is.

148
00:13:19,699 --> 00:13:24,004
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you've seen it enough that it pertains to... that it shares exactly the same nature.

149
00:13:24,585 --> 00:13:28,710
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if all these things of that nature are obvious subject to change,

150
00:13:31,697 --> 00:13:34,623
[SPEAKER_00]: Nothing else, then, that shows that nature cannot escape it.

151
00:13:35,405 --> 00:13:42,480
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's how you include, that's how you contemplate this... the four elements, in that sense, that would result in this passion.

152
00:13:43,801 --> 00:13:49,602
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the entire world of passion exists when you're ignoring the peripheral and being absorbed in the object of your senses.

153
00:13:49,742 --> 00:14:00,865
[SPEAKER_00]: Obviously, being mesmerized and trapped through the pleasure that you get, through avoidance and aversion towards pain, offers of management, offers of escape and so on.

154
00:14:00,885 --> 00:14:05,326
[SPEAKER_00]: You keep overlooking the bigger picture, the experience as a whole, how we say it.

155
00:14:06,126 --> 00:14:11,927
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why even if you tell yourself, oh, yes, I know this body is like these great elements, you're not really feeling it on that level.

156
00:14:13,898 --> 00:14:21,827
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the real contemplation is, yes, contemplate how these great elements change, how you cannot be exempt from that, and then feel it.

157
00:14:22,588 --> 00:14:24,210
[SPEAKER_00]: Feel how you cannot be exempt from that.

158
00:14:25,632 --> 00:14:29,977
[SPEAKER_00]: And don't try to then psychologize and get rid of that uncomfortable feeling that might come up.

159
00:14:31,057 --> 00:14:31,197
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

160
00:14:31,377 --> 00:14:32,257
[SPEAKER_00]: Just leave it there.

161
00:14:32,757 --> 00:14:37,159
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's how it feels to take something that's not yours as yours.

162
00:14:37,239 --> 00:14:38,219
[SPEAKER_00]: To appropriate it.

163
00:14:38,239 --> 00:14:39,379
[SPEAKER_00]: It feels dangerous.

164
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:43,440
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't try to, oh, I must get rid of this danger because it's unpleasant.

165
00:14:43,541 --> 00:14:44,441
[SPEAKER_00]: I must concentrate.

166
00:14:44,461 --> 00:14:45,181
[SPEAKER_00]: I must meditate.

167
00:14:45,221 --> 00:14:46,521
[SPEAKER_00]: I must calm down or something.

168
00:14:47,722 --> 00:14:47,822
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

169
00:14:47,942 --> 00:14:50,763
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't make it worse, but at the same time recognize, no, no, no.

170
00:14:50,863 --> 00:14:56,024
[SPEAKER_00]: This danger is there, affecting me only because I'm taking what I shouldn't be taking up.

171
00:14:57,424 --> 00:14:59,225
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you leave it there long enough,

172
00:15:00,265 --> 00:15:01,266
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't try to get rid of it.

173
00:15:01,386 --> 00:15:02,688
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't act out of it for sure.

174
00:15:03,589 --> 00:15:04,470
[SPEAKER_00]: You stop taking it.

175
00:15:06,313 --> 00:15:10,058
[SPEAKER_00]: When the danger doesn't touch you anymore, you know you would have let go of the bait.

176
00:15:12,721 --> 00:15:14,944
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's the earth, water, fire, same.

177
00:15:16,403 --> 00:15:16,803
[SPEAKER_00]: Whichever.

178
00:15:16,843 --> 00:15:19,145
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't even have to go out to earth and then water.

179
00:15:19,165 --> 00:15:20,966
[SPEAKER_00]: Just take any or a different day.

180
00:15:21,046 --> 00:15:22,047
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't matter.

181
00:15:22,107 --> 00:15:23,668
[SPEAKER_00]: They all stand for the same principle.

182
00:15:23,748 --> 00:15:26,610
[SPEAKER_00]: They all stand for that same peripheral that's usually being overlooked.

183
00:15:27,091 --> 00:15:32,634
[SPEAKER_00]: They all stand for that lack of or insufficient yonison, to say, to put it that way.

184
00:15:33,715 --> 00:15:40,359
[SPEAKER_00]: And the space element is included because, yes, it's not primary on the level of the four elements, but it's it's practical.

185
00:15:40,419 --> 00:15:44,482
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, you could see everything else and then you could kind of see or even think space in between.

186
00:15:44,942 --> 00:15:51,066
[SPEAKER_00]: So, now you include the space in between as the element, as the thing that changed, that's defined by things that's in space and so on.

187
00:15:51,767 --> 00:15:55,209
[SPEAKER_00]: Either way, the point is you can't appropriate it, even if you want to.

188
00:15:55,689 --> 00:16:02,714
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you want to then recognize that that which you do appropriate, your internal sense bases, eyes, ears, nose, body and so on,

189
00:16:03,674 --> 00:16:06,296
[SPEAKER_00]: That too cannot be appropriated, even if you want to.

190
00:16:07,297 --> 00:16:09,698
[SPEAKER_00]: But it will take a while for that to sink in.

191
00:16:10,559 --> 00:16:23,307
[SPEAKER_00]: And for the duration of that whole practice, you need to have been and sustain your withdrawal from unwholesome states, virtue, restraint and everything else.

192
00:16:23,407 --> 00:16:26,149
[SPEAKER_00]: Just without it, it's like, well, you're not going to get anywhere.

193
00:16:28,638 --> 00:16:40,306
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, these kind of more poetic similes develop your mind like earth, develop yourself like water, like fire, in the same, basically, the context you strive for.

194
00:16:41,586 --> 00:16:45,469
[SPEAKER_00]: If the whole thing is unownable, means the whole thing is not yours, means the whole thing is not your problem.

195
00:16:46,010 --> 00:16:52,434
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whatever your eyes see, hear, smell, taste, touch, you won't be desiring it and you certainly won't be repelled by it, because it's not your problem.

196
00:16:55,588 --> 00:16:57,309
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, he goes on to develop friendliness.

197
00:16:57,889 --> 00:17:01,551
[SPEAKER_00]: If we develop friendliness, any ill will will be abandoned.

198
00:17:02,171 --> 00:17:06,774
[SPEAKER_00]: Maybe we can address that later, these four brahma-vihāras.

199
00:17:07,194 --> 00:17:10,836
[SPEAKER_00]: So, let's go back to the recollection of the breathing, then.

200
00:17:10,856 --> 00:17:14,478
[SPEAKER_00]: It says, so it will be obviously very fruitful and beneficial.

201
00:17:14,778 --> 00:17:18,521
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, it goes to the standard description, at the end of it, saying

202
00:17:19,561 --> 00:17:32,794
[SPEAKER_00]: When a bhikkhu gone to wilderness, the roof of a tree... the roof of a tree... the root of a tree, or to an empty hut... Where was I?

203
00:17:32,814 --> 00:17:36,157
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yeah, the screen changed.

204
00:17:37,434 --> 00:17:47,687
[SPEAKER_00]: So, gone to wilderness or to root of a tree or an empty hut, sits down cross-legged, sets the body straight and establishes a recollection at the fore.

205
00:17:47,927 --> 00:17:49,048
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollected, he breathes in.

206
00:17:49,228 --> 00:17:50,330
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollected, he breathes out.

207
00:17:51,681 --> 00:17:53,062
[SPEAKER_00]: Breathing in long, he understands.

208
00:17:53,082 --> 00:17:53,822
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm breathing in long.

209
00:17:54,023 --> 00:17:55,223
[SPEAKER_00]: Breathing out long, he understands.

210
00:17:55,243 --> 00:17:56,004
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm breathing out long.

211
00:17:56,404 --> 00:17:57,985
[SPEAKER_00]: Breathing in short, he understands.

212
00:17:58,005 --> 00:17:58,826
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm breathing in short.

213
00:17:59,086 --> 00:18:00,427
[SPEAKER_00]: Breathing out short, he understands.

214
00:18:00,467 --> 00:18:01,268
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm breathing out short.

215
00:18:01,868 --> 00:18:02,548
[SPEAKER_00]: He trains like this.

216
00:18:02,709 --> 00:18:04,410
[SPEAKER_00]: Experiencing the whole body, I'll breathe in.

217
00:18:05,310 --> 00:18:06,031
[SPEAKER_00]: He trains like this.

218
00:18:06,071 --> 00:18:07,592
[SPEAKER_00]: Experiencing the whole body, I'll breathe out.

219
00:18:08,713 --> 00:18:10,414
[SPEAKER_00]: Calming the bodily activity, I'll breathe in.

220
00:18:10,634 --> 00:18:12,515
[SPEAKER_00]: He trains calming the bodily activity, I'll breathe out.

221
00:18:13,356 --> 00:18:14,837
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can already see

222
00:18:16,929 --> 00:18:18,089
[SPEAKER_00]: How it starts?

223
00:18:18,109 --> 00:18:18,770
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollected.

224
00:18:19,290 --> 00:18:21,571
[SPEAKER_00]: So, non-forgetfully, he breathes in.

225
00:18:21,891 --> 00:18:23,511
[SPEAKER_00]: Non-forgetfully, he breathes out.

226
00:18:24,512 --> 00:18:26,032
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the practice in and of itself.

227
00:18:27,293 --> 00:18:30,774
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no new steps that you add to this.

228
00:18:30,934 --> 00:18:34,075
[SPEAKER_00]: Everything else that follows is within this this thing.

229
00:18:35,923 --> 00:18:37,184
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollected, he breathes in.

230
00:18:37,264 --> 00:18:38,484
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollected, he breathes out.

231
00:18:38,945 --> 00:18:39,985
[SPEAKER_00]: That doesn't change.

232
00:18:40,846 --> 00:18:51,952
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you think... if you go to the next step, quote-unquote, I'll breathe in long, and you already lost your recollection, you are not breathing in long with understanding.

233
00:18:53,073 --> 00:18:57,495
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in other words, practice recollectively breathing in, recollectively breathing out,

234
00:19:00,691 --> 00:19:03,212
[SPEAKER_00]: That's kind of the whole point.

235
00:19:04,232 --> 00:19:12,335
[SPEAKER_00]: In order to know that you're already breathing, you don't need to concentrate on the parts of your body to reveal to you that you're already breathing.

236
00:19:12,375 --> 00:19:15,757
[SPEAKER_00]: The knowledge that you're breathing is already there, so don't forget it.

237
00:19:16,357 --> 00:19:18,598
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't forget that the body is already breathing.

238
00:19:18,978 --> 00:19:20,299
[SPEAKER_00]: See it at the back of your mind.

239
00:19:20,399 --> 00:19:26,742
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't stop doing things in the sense of, like, I don't know, if you're walking or sitting or something.

240
00:19:26,763 --> 00:19:39,709
[SPEAKER_00]: Obviously, you can't be too occupied with your attention, like reading and doing stuff that would take too much of your attention, but you don't have to concentrate on top of withdrawing from activities in order to see what's already there.

241
00:19:39,749 --> 00:19:42,691
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't need to concentrate on your breath to know that it's there.

242
00:19:43,572 --> 00:19:51,738
[SPEAKER_00]: So, just go to a non-disturbed, like, quiet place and bring your mindfulness to the fore, as I said, parimukam.

243
00:19:51,999 --> 00:19:59,284
[SPEAKER_00]: The point is just, okay, stop being distracted and sit down and recognize what's already there.

244
00:20:00,225 --> 00:20:06,150
[SPEAKER_00]: So, let that memory of your breath that's happening right there while you're remembering it,

245
00:20:06,939 --> 00:20:08,781
[SPEAKER_00]: Let it... let it be there, in the peripheral.

246
00:20:08,821 --> 00:20:09,482
[SPEAKER_00]: Let it endure.

247
00:20:09,742 --> 00:20:13,746
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't have to... okay, now I do this, and now I do that, and where does that lead?

248
00:20:14,166 --> 00:20:14,506
[SPEAKER_00]: No, no, no.

249
00:20:14,767 --> 00:20:15,427
[SPEAKER_00]: It leads nowhere.

250
00:20:15,467 --> 00:20:17,790
[SPEAKER_00]: Leads there... where it begins, that's where it ends.

251
00:20:18,490 --> 00:20:21,473
[SPEAKER_00]: It begins with recollect the hybrids in, recollect the hybrids out.

252
00:20:21,713 --> 00:20:22,875
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the beginning and the end.

253
00:20:24,877 --> 00:20:28,340
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I know that there's a tendency to overthink it, because obviously

254
00:20:29,917 --> 00:20:42,464
[SPEAKER_00]: All the contemporary meditations, and not just even Buddhists, have mystified the breath long enough, and now there is all these implicit assumptions and hopes and tendencies associated with this practice.

255
00:20:42,524 --> 00:20:45,826
[SPEAKER_00]: But really, mindfully he breathes in, mindfully he breathes out.

256
00:20:46,146 --> 00:20:48,467
[SPEAKER_00]: Non-forgetfully he breathes in, non-forgetfully he breathes out.

257
00:20:48,527 --> 00:20:49,228
[SPEAKER_00]: See how that feels.

258
00:20:49,548 --> 00:20:54,030
[SPEAKER_00]: Just sit down and let the body breathe, and try to not completely forget about it.

259
00:20:55,251 --> 00:20:58,593
[SPEAKER_00]: The mind will come up with stuff, but don't completely

260
00:20:59,543 --> 00:21:00,083
[SPEAKER_00]: Drift away.

261
00:21:00,403 --> 00:21:01,064
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the point.

262
00:21:04,806 --> 00:21:06,186
[SPEAKER_00]: As the other suttas do say that.

263
00:21:06,426 --> 00:21:10,028
[SPEAKER_00]: I think it was that Arita Sutta, in Majjhima or somewhere, I don't remember.

264
00:21:10,468 --> 00:21:13,431
[SPEAKER_00]: We said, basically, this is how he practices the breathing.

265
00:21:13,491 --> 00:21:14,432
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollected, he breathes in.

266
00:21:14,492 --> 00:21:15,493
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollected, he breathes out.

267
00:21:15,873 --> 00:21:17,655
[SPEAKER_00]: He abandons all the patiga.

268
00:21:17,715 --> 00:21:21,078
[SPEAKER_00]: He abandons sensuality of the past and the future and present.

269
00:21:21,838 --> 00:21:24,521
[SPEAKER_00]: And all the patiga in regard to the body has also been abandoned.

270
00:21:24,581 --> 00:21:25,622
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how he fulfills it.

271
00:21:25,662 --> 00:21:28,564
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Buddha says, yeah, sure, that is obviously the way.

272
00:21:29,065 --> 00:21:30,606
[SPEAKER_00]: However, it's not complete.

273
00:21:31,027 --> 00:21:36,472
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he goes to expound on these other additional steps, which are not steps.

274
00:21:36,992 --> 00:21:44,739
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just refinements of the... refinement aspects of the same principle, which is recollected, breathe in, recollected, breathe out.

275
00:21:45,780 --> 00:22:01,053
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if that becomes established, like, in other words, when... doesn't matter how much your attention shifts and goes from here to there, in the back of your mind, if it's been broadened enough, there's always going to be at least a grain of recognition that there is breathing in and breathing out.

276
00:22:01,233 --> 00:22:01,553
[SPEAKER_00]: That's it.

277
00:22:03,122 --> 00:22:05,504
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's how you would then... you could refine that.

278
00:22:05,784 --> 00:22:14,269
[SPEAKER_00]: So now, within that peripheral recognition of breathing in, breathing out, you would recognize that you're breathing in long, that you're breathing out long.

279
00:22:14,329 --> 00:22:15,790
[SPEAKER_00]: Before, it was just breathing in and out.

280
00:22:15,850 --> 00:22:19,312
[SPEAKER_00]: Doesn't matter how... it was too much, basically, to discern that.

281
00:22:20,013 --> 00:22:20,913
[SPEAKER_00]: But now you can discern.

282
00:22:21,534 --> 00:22:23,735
[SPEAKER_00]: You can discern that it's long, you can discern that it's short.

283
00:22:25,449 --> 00:22:27,029
[SPEAKER_00]: And, eh... and you understand that.

284
00:22:27,309 --> 00:22:27,710
[SPEAKER_00]: You see it.

285
00:22:27,850 --> 00:22:29,830
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't need to... you don't need to attend to it.

286
00:22:30,030 --> 00:22:31,890
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't need to monitor every second of it.

287
00:22:32,051 --> 00:22:32,711
[SPEAKER_00]: Quite the opposite.

288
00:22:32,731 --> 00:22:36,211
[SPEAKER_00]: If you do, you will lose the sight of it.

289
00:22:36,231 --> 00:22:45,954
[SPEAKER_00]: That's kind of the point of the entire... any practice of sati is to unabsorb you from... from... from your senses, from your observations, from your overly concentrated attitude.

290
00:22:46,574 --> 00:22:52,015
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why I keep saying modern meditations and practices are taking you in the completely opposite direction of where the dhamma is.

291
00:22:53,466 --> 00:23:10,357
[SPEAKER_00]: So, once you define even that, like now, peripherally, not just that you know you're breathing in, not just that you're not forgetting that you're breathing out, you are also knowing and understanding that you're breathing in long, and that you're breathing out long, that you're breathing in short, that you're breathing out short.

292
00:23:11,078 --> 00:23:13,700
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the knowledge of that has been even modified.

293
00:23:13,740 --> 00:23:20,144
[SPEAKER_00]: In other words, the sight, the range of your peripheral, without needing to attend to it directly, has been expanded.

294
00:23:21,425 --> 00:23:22,926
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, you can train further.

295
00:23:24,054 --> 00:23:24,855
[SPEAKER_00]: He trains like this.

296
00:23:24,935 --> 00:23:26,856
[SPEAKER_00]: Experiencing the whole body, I'll breathe in.

297
00:23:27,596 --> 00:23:28,297
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what does that mean?

298
00:23:28,317 --> 00:23:37,743
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that means that within the memory of the in-breath that is happening right now, I shall outline this internal body.

299
00:23:38,343 --> 00:23:41,886
[SPEAKER_00]: This body that is previous paragraph would have been talking about.

300
00:23:43,166 --> 00:23:45,568
[SPEAKER_00]: So, as I said, the internal body is always overlooked.

301
00:23:46,427 --> 00:23:52,849
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why, through developing ānāpānasati correctly, in this indirect method, you are developing the peripheral.

302
00:23:52,869 --> 00:23:57,950
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means, whether you want it or not, you are developing the internal recognition of the internal body.

303
00:23:58,550 --> 00:24:10,774
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you could now make the actual, like a more active effort, that within that peripheral, you discern the extent of your physicality, without needing to directly attend to it.

304
00:24:10,794 --> 00:24:15,335
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if you do, it's not the body you're seeing, it's the objects of your senses, of your body.

305
00:24:16,135 --> 00:24:17,936
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why he trains like this.

306
00:24:19,276 --> 00:24:34,122
[SPEAKER_00]: In other words, make the effort to peripherally, once you become familiar with it, outline that which body is, that full sphere of internal, that which is, that nature of these four great elements externally, that are obviously changing, and so on.

307
00:24:35,362 --> 00:24:37,863
[SPEAKER_00]: So, experiencing the whole body, I'll breathe in.

308
00:24:37,943 --> 00:24:39,764
[SPEAKER_00]: Experiencing the whole body, I'll breathe out.

309
00:24:41,114 --> 00:24:49,699
[SPEAKER_00]: So, see, you don't calm the bodily activity without even recognizing the extent of that body.

310
00:24:50,219 --> 00:24:55,562
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't calm your physicality if you don't even see the phenomenon of physicality there, peripherally.

311
00:24:56,582 --> 00:25:00,284
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's why, once you see it, now you could actually calm it.

312
00:25:03,130 --> 00:25:04,751
[SPEAKER_00]: So, calming the bodily activity, I'll breathe in.

313
00:25:05,171 --> 00:25:06,471
[SPEAKER_00]: Calming the bodily activity, I'll breathe out.

314
00:25:07,231 --> 00:25:10,873
[SPEAKER_00]: Those are, by the way, still all refinements of this very thing.

315
00:25:11,033 --> 00:25:12,013
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollected, he breathes in.

316
00:25:12,133 --> 00:25:13,133
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollected, he breathes out.

317
00:25:14,014 --> 00:25:15,194
[SPEAKER_00]: They are not extra steps.

318
00:25:16,494 --> 00:25:17,395
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, he trains like this.

319
00:25:17,615 --> 00:25:19,135
[SPEAKER_00]: Experiencing joy, I'll breathe in.

320
00:25:19,435 --> 00:25:20,676
[SPEAKER_00]: Experiencing joy, I'll breathe out.

321
00:25:20,756 --> 00:25:24,217
[SPEAKER_00]: See, now you're getting even on a subtler level, which is not even

322
00:25:25,821 --> 00:25:27,783
[SPEAKER_00]: You're not so concerned with physicality anymore.

323
00:25:28,403 --> 00:25:45,938
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, you should just train... See, if you would have refined your indirect attention on that peripheral level, to the point of calming the physicality without direct falling into a trap of directly attending to it, you could now just experience joy.

324
00:25:45,958 --> 00:25:50,882
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, generate joy on the level of those feelings there, peripherally.

325
00:25:52,287 --> 00:25:53,667
[SPEAKER_00]: So, experiencing joy, I'll breathe in.

326
00:25:53,967 --> 00:25:55,268
[SPEAKER_00]: Experiencing joy, I'll breathe out.

327
00:25:56,088 --> 00:25:57,368
[SPEAKER_00]: Experiencing ease, I'll breathe in.

328
00:25:57,728 --> 00:25:59,068
[SPEAKER_00]: Experiencing ease, I'll breathe out.

329
00:26:00,449 --> 00:26:02,249
[SPEAKER_00]: So, these are kind of precursors.

330
00:26:02,289 --> 00:26:10,730
[SPEAKER_00]: Basically, it's about the feelings that are obviously, as I said before, they're kind of neither in your physicality nor on the level where your mind is, but they're factually there.

331
00:26:10,790 --> 00:26:18,292
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when the physicality is tamed enough, sufficiently discerned on that peripheral level,

332
00:26:19,496 --> 00:26:23,799
[SPEAKER_00]: What's left there, whatever's felt there, you could then actually calm it.

333
00:26:24,760 --> 00:26:25,841
[SPEAKER_00]: You could ease it.

334
00:26:27,542 --> 00:26:30,264
[SPEAKER_00]: You could be joyful in it, so to speak.

335
00:26:30,304 --> 00:26:32,366
[SPEAKER_00]: You could experience happiness on account of it.

336
00:26:32,386 --> 00:26:34,227
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it's already quite purified, obviously.

337
00:26:35,408 --> 00:26:38,290
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, the next step is experiencing the mind activity.

338
00:26:38,830 --> 00:26:42,213
[SPEAKER_00]: In other words, you're gonna find your mind active.

339
00:26:42,973 --> 00:26:46,176
[SPEAKER_00]: That citta, that animal, will have some activity to some extent.

340
00:26:47,467 --> 00:26:48,909
[SPEAKER_00]: And you want to outline that.

341
00:26:49,509 --> 00:27:01,223
[SPEAKER_00]: Just as you were outlining the whole body, just as you were outlining the feelings through joy and ease, now you're outlining the mind, experiencing the mind activity.

342
00:27:02,358 --> 00:27:03,580
[SPEAKER_00]: Why do you need to outline the mind?

343
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:19,880
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, outlining the mind, in a very accurate sense, on that far developed peripheral level, that you are seeing on that internal... in that internal dimension, to put it that way, experiencing, discerning, outlining the mind,

344
00:27:20,952 --> 00:27:22,193
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a precursor to step two.

345
00:27:22,253 --> 00:27:22,993
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, you could calm it.

346
00:27:23,653 --> 00:27:26,334
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, you could really just calm that animal down.

347
00:27:26,434 --> 00:27:28,655
[SPEAKER_00]: Just tell it to, okay, sit down.

348
00:27:29,355 --> 00:27:32,217
[SPEAKER_00]: While I breathe in, I shall be seating this this mind.

349
00:27:32,737 --> 00:27:34,998
[SPEAKER_00]: While I breathe out, I shall be seating it further.

350
00:27:35,438 --> 00:27:36,738
[SPEAKER_00]: So, until it just calms down.

351
00:27:38,199 --> 00:27:42,881
[SPEAKER_00]: Once it's completely calm, seated, it is, you can experience it even more.

352
00:27:44,060 --> 00:27:48,103
[SPEAKER_00]: As in, outline it clearer, in its calm, immovable state.

353
00:27:49,124 --> 00:27:50,585
[SPEAKER_00]: So, experience in the mind, I'll breathe in.

354
00:27:50,625 --> 00:27:52,006
[SPEAKER_00]: Experience in the mind, I'll breathe out.

355
00:27:52,467 --> 00:27:53,368
[SPEAKER_00]: Gladdening the mind.

356
00:27:53,688 --> 00:27:55,109
[SPEAKER_00]: Literally, gladdening the animal.

357
00:27:55,870 --> 00:27:56,690
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, gladden it.

358
00:27:56,770 --> 00:27:57,291
[SPEAKER_00]: Uplift it.

359
00:27:57,951 --> 00:28:11,222
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you are on the level of directly communicating to it through your indirect development of not directly attending to the peripheral level where you've been discerning these things more and more and more.

360
00:28:12,758 --> 00:28:24,084
[SPEAKER_00]: So, once you calm the mind, once you outline the mind, once you calm it, once you gladden it, you can compose it, you can liberate it, you could tell it, basically, turn away.

361
00:28:24,624 --> 00:28:30,147
[SPEAKER_00]: Turn away from everything that you've been going after, because both of us see now that it's not worth it.

362
00:28:30,788 --> 00:28:34,830
[SPEAKER_00]: And the mind will listen, because you have showed it that it's not worth it.

363
00:28:35,390 --> 00:28:36,731
[SPEAKER_00]: How you show that it's not worth it?

364
00:28:36,791 --> 00:28:40,013
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you showed it through the perception of impermanence,

365
00:28:40,997 --> 00:28:45,970
[SPEAKER_00]: Perception of non-beauty, development of friendliness, compassion, contentment, equanimity.

366
00:28:46,431 --> 00:28:47,755
[SPEAKER_00]: But anyway, we'll deal with it later.

367
00:28:49,312 --> 00:28:51,814
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he goes here to do the same, actually.

368
00:28:52,014 --> 00:28:53,054
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he trains further.

369
00:28:53,575 --> 00:29:02,660
[SPEAKER_00]: Now that the mind is being liberated, and it's listening, and it's composed, you then maintain the perspective of impermanence, while you breathe in.

370
00:29:03,141 --> 00:29:13,167
[SPEAKER_00]: So, while breathe in, while breathe out, just means, basically, it's another way of saying, the peripheral dimension discerned through not directly attending it, maintains.

371
00:29:13,667 --> 00:29:14,307
[SPEAKER_00]: It's maintained.

372
00:29:14,427 --> 00:29:15,008
[SPEAKER_00]: It endures.

373
00:29:15,528 --> 00:29:19,131
[SPEAKER_00]: So, within that, you now think of impermanence.

374
00:29:19,712 --> 00:29:24,155
[SPEAKER_00]: Within that, you think of dispassion, you think of cessation, you think of relinquishment.

375
00:29:24,555 --> 00:29:32,102
[SPEAKER_00]: These are the perceptions that now are directly talking to your mind, which is also over there, peripherally, where that physicality is.

376
00:29:32,462 --> 00:29:36,685
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is why you started with physicality and feelings and so on, before you were able to outline the mind.

377
00:29:37,626 --> 00:29:39,348
[SPEAKER_00]: Fully, obviously, you've got some idea.

378
00:29:40,209 --> 00:29:44,196
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why, when recollection of breathing, when developed in Kālta, in this way, it's very fruitful, beneficial.

379
00:29:44,236 --> 00:29:46,561
[SPEAKER_00]: In other words, there'll be nothing that you haven't addressed.

380
00:29:48,425 --> 00:29:53,647
[SPEAKER_00]: And when the recollection of breathing is developed and cultivated this way, even one's final breath ceases knowingly, not unknowingly.

381
00:29:54,307 --> 00:30:05,231
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if ānāpānasati is to be understood, how people think of it today, as I must concentrate on my breath in order to know it, you're never going to be able to know your final breath, because death always comes as a surprise.

382
00:30:05,951 --> 00:30:09,933
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is the very exact point that the Buddha wants to illustrate here, is that

383
00:30:11,455 --> 00:30:23,279
[SPEAKER_00]: Even final breath, which is always a surprise to an untrained mind, cannot not be included in that sufficiently developed peripheral recognition of non-directly attending to your breathing, yet knowing that it's there.

384
00:30:24,040 --> 00:30:35,083
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you would have developed that thoroughly, on a day-to-day basis, even the utmost surprise cannot make you not see that that extent.

385
00:30:35,864 --> 00:30:39,005
[SPEAKER_00]: Cannot make you not... Can you make you lose perspective and ignore it?

386
00:30:40,043 --> 00:30:42,765
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even the last breath will be known.

387
00:30:43,426 --> 00:30:48,690
[SPEAKER_00]: Not because you'll be waiting, hunting for it there, to not miss it, like a bullet train or something.

388
00:30:49,130 --> 00:30:49,250
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

389
00:30:49,350 --> 00:30:50,991
[SPEAKER_00]: It will be known, because it will be included.

390
00:30:51,112 --> 00:30:53,914
[SPEAKER_00]: It will be included, because your mind has already surmounted the whole thing.

391
00:30:55,075 --> 00:30:57,697
[SPEAKER_00]: It's in front of it, how you pretty much started the practice.

392
00:30:59,218 --> 00:31:00,218
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's what the Buddha said.

393
00:31:00,719 --> 00:31:04,222
[SPEAKER_00]: Venerable Rahula was obviously very pleased.

394
00:31:06,323 --> 00:31:08,405
[SPEAKER_00]: So, let me just...

395
00:31:10,516 --> 00:31:11,357
[SPEAKER_00]: And just a few more things.

396
00:31:12,717 --> 00:31:12,938
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

397
00:31:13,398 --> 00:31:15,999
[SPEAKER_00]: So, back on to the friendliness.

398
00:31:16,400 --> 00:31:23,564
[SPEAKER_00]: And, like, it's kind of like, oh, develop friendliness to abandon the ill-will.

399
00:31:24,405 --> 00:31:26,286
[SPEAKER_00]: So people think, aha, see, so I do metta.

400
00:31:26,966 --> 00:31:28,287
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, develop friendliness.

401
00:31:28,347 --> 00:31:30,388
[SPEAKER_00]: Nobody says you shouldn't develop it.

402
00:31:30,648 --> 00:31:33,290
[SPEAKER_00]: It's how you develop it, what you do about it.

403
00:31:33,330 --> 00:31:37,653
[SPEAKER_00]: Does develop friendliness mean go and think positive thoughts about people that you hate?

404
00:31:38,860 --> 00:31:40,701
[SPEAKER_00]: But does that mean your hate came from those people?

405
00:31:41,961 --> 00:31:44,342
[SPEAKER_00]: So, does your real will come from people that upset you?

406
00:31:48,403 --> 00:31:53,165
[SPEAKER_00]: If not, then why do you need to think positive thoughts of those people when they are not the problem?

407
00:31:55,305 --> 00:31:57,526
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if your real will does come from those people, well...

408
00:31:58,705 --> 00:31:59,705
[SPEAKER_00]: Good luck overcoming it.

409
00:31:59,926 --> 00:32:02,127
[SPEAKER_00]: Because their actions will never be in your control.

410
00:32:02,167 --> 00:32:06,829
[SPEAKER_00]: And if their actions are truly the cause, the beginning of your real will, you can never uproot it.

411
00:32:06,869 --> 00:32:10,170
[SPEAKER_00]: You can only put a perfect patch on it every time it comes up.

412
00:32:11,411 --> 00:32:13,172
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yes, develop friendliness.

413
00:32:13,372 --> 00:32:18,134
[SPEAKER_00]: But that still doesn't justify the contemporary ideas of Metta, which are absolutely ridiculous.

414
00:32:20,155 --> 00:32:21,896
[SPEAKER_00]: So, how do you then develop friendliness?

415
00:32:22,636 --> 00:32:24,657
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, by recognizing the roots of your aversion.

416
00:32:26,338 --> 00:32:27,722
[SPEAKER_00]: And what is the root of your aversion?

417
00:32:27,762 --> 00:32:30,810
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's your own resistance to your own sense basis.

418
00:32:32,667 --> 00:32:36,849
[SPEAKER_00]: So, first, it's not sense-objects.

419
00:32:36,909 --> 00:32:39,290
[SPEAKER_00]: Therefore, others or non-others, it's absolutely irrelevant.

420
00:32:40,290 --> 00:32:50,815
[SPEAKER_00]: Second, if you are not withdrawn from sense-objects fully, thoroughly, through virtue and restraint, you're not even going to outline the the internal dimension, as we just been through, as we just discussed.

421
00:32:51,555 --> 00:33:02,440
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there is a reason the Buddha said these practices after, like, you would have been outlining everything through the peripheral recognition of the nature of the elements that your own physicality partakes in.

422
00:33:04,203 --> 00:33:10,446
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, when you are basically... say, you would have been practicing those contemplations regularly.

423
00:33:10,466 --> 00:33:29,995
[SPEAKER_00]: You wanna... you wanna sit down and meditate, contemplate, sit down and start pondering on this nature, start developing the peripheral discernment, including things into it, so... so that nothing is left out, so that you don't even have to go around thinking about those things actively through your focused attention, because they'll be on the level of the knowledge now.

424
00:33:30,075 --> 00:33:31,416
[SPEAKER_00]: They're known, they're understood.

425
00:33:31,616 --> 00:33:33,657
[SPEAKER_00]: You can go about your day knowing those things.

426
00:33:34,642 --> 00:33:40,728
[SPEAKER_00]: So, once you would have practiced that, then, yes, you could then also, on that same indirect level, practice friendliness.

427
00:33:41,528 --> 00:33:46,393
[SPEAKER_00]: Literally, develop the non-ill-will towards your own sense bases.

428
00:33:47,693 --> 00:33:55,258
[SPEAKER_00]: So, these sense bases, these sense domains, they have their own feeding grounds, as I should say.

429
00:33:56,058 --> 00:34:02,762
[SPEAKER_00]: When the sight, sound, smell, taste, touches, sensations land, if they're uncomfortable, you twitch.

430
00:34:03,623 --> 00:34:04,764
[SPEAKER_00]: The sense bases twitch.

431
00:34:05,444 --> 00:34:06,405
[SPEAKER_00]: You are averse to that.

432
00:34:08,306 --> 00:34:09,907
[SPEAKER_00]: There is resistance, there is patīgā.

433
00:34:10,887 --> 00:34:11,968
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the root of all hate.

434
00:34:13,897 --> 00:34:19,059
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, you wouldn't be able to hate your neighbor who said something upsetting if you didn't hear what he said.

435
00:34:20,839 --> 00:34:22,820
[SPEAKER_00]: But, obviously, those levels are not seen.

436
00:34:23,040 --> 00:34:24,200
[SPEAKER_00]: So, all you see is the neighbor.

437
00:34:24,800 --> 00:34:26,101
[SPEAKER_00]: All you see is his intentions.

438
00:34:26,141 --> 00:34:30,622
[SPEAKER_00]: All you see is how he's been doing this all the time, you know, and you just keep winding yourself up around your own projected views.

439
00:34:31,362 --> 00:34:36,964
[SPEAKER_00]: But, fundamentally, it's really your own ears, eyes, nose, body that you're resisting.

440
00:34:37,744 --> 00:34:40,105
[SPEAKER_00]: That is what the root of your aversion is.

441
00:34:40,900 --> 00:34:42,642
[SPEAKER_00]: So, spread matter to yourself.

442
00:34:43,143 --> 00:34:54,196
[SPEAKER_00]: Not, in a sense, love yourself, because that would be equally ignorant, but recognize that the aversion comes from you not being trained in regard to your own internal, internal sense bases.

443
00:34:54,697 --> 00:35:00,304
[SPEAKER_00]: These things that, that, that sight, sound, smell, taste, touches land on, so to speak.

444
00:35:01,504 --> 00:35:18,749
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you choose to, on that... see, like, if you would have been developing in regard to physicality rightly, now you could say... you could be recognizing the internal domains, you know, where... where the pressure comes up, where the aversion manifests, and not be averse towards that.

445
00:35:19,850 --> 00:35:23,991
[SPEAKER_00]: So, don't be averse towards that pang of aversion that happens internally.

446
00:35:24,836 --> 00:35:32,962
[SPEAKER_00]: But by that point, obviously, you would have had to stop blaming the world, stop blaming others, even if it's like, you know, the most justifiable thing to do.

447
00:35:33,002 --> 00:35:35,344
[SPEAKER_00]: It's because of, you know, what he said, she did or something.

448
00:35:35,884 --> 00:35:37,565
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, all of that is second.

449
00:35:38,166 --> 00:35:43,630
[SPEAKER_00]: The root of aversion, it's always my own resistance to my own sense bases, sense organs.

450
00:35:44,070 --> 00:35:44,951
[SPEAKER_00]: You can say it that way.

451
00:35:45,731 --> 00:35:53,237
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's pretty much what triggers everything else that then proliferates and spreads and gets projected onto the world and actions that follow.

452
00:35:54,117 --> 00:36:02,163
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you develop non-resistance, if you develop friendliness, just be a friend towards your own internal senses when they are averse.

453
00:36:02,963 --> 00:36:08,767
[SPEAKER_00]: Just like a friend say, okay, you know, let's not make this worse, let's not act out of it.

454
00:36:09,288 --> 00:36:09,788
[SPEAKER_00]: Calm down.

455
00:36:10,008 --> 00:36:12,870
[SPEAKER_00]: The mind's gonna come up and says, no, no, no, but it's because of his saying.

456
00:36:12,890 --> 00:36:16,993
[SPEAKER_00]: If you don't do anything about it, he'll do it again and they'll do it again and the whole thing will go through.

457
00:36:17,013 --> 00:36:17,934
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like, it doesn't matter.

458
00:36:18,014 --> 00:36:18,955
[SPEAKER_00]: All of those are traps.

459
00:36:19,715 --> 00:36:30,960
[SPEAKER_00]: All of those are to make me act towards it and overlook where the real problem is, which is my own aversion towards this internal thing that I have not been trained myself in regard to.

460
00:36:32,361 --> 00:36:39,144
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you do, again, there's absolutely nothing that can come from the world that could surprise you or make you overlook that.

461
00:36:39,864 --> 00:36:43,226
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you would be abandoning ill will by killing it at its roots.

462
00:36:45,752 --> 00:36:48,794
[SPEAKER_00]: And the same goes for the other four brahma-vihāras.

463
00:36:48,834 --> 00:36:59,002
[SPEAKER_00]: The point is, they're all developed on that progressively more refined state of the peripheral, of the discernment, what's internal, and further, and further, and further.

464
00:36:59,522 --> 00:37:05,146
[SPEAKER_00]: But, yeah, just stick with metta, if you want, on that level, and you will be unable to hate.

465
00:37:05,506 --> 00:37:10,550
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the framework of non-hate towards the root, towards the trigger of aversion,

466
00:37:11,635 --> 00:37:14,736
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is your sense bases when they encounter things that are disagreeable.

467
00:37:15,737 --> 00:37:16,777
[SPEAKER_00]: That framework doesn't change.

468
00:37:16,817 --> 00:37:19,218
[SPEAKER_00]: That framework is now unfaltering.

469
00:37:19,378 --> 00:37:21,779
[SPEAKER_00]: That framework cannot be lost.

470
00:37:22,540 --> 00:37:29,803
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, again, you have a direct verification that no amount of pressure can touch you.

471
00:37:30,323 --> 00:37:34,305
[SPEAKER_00]: No amount of pressure can cause that aversion and snowball into actions and so on.

472
00:37:35,553 --> 00:37:41,555
[SPEAKER_00]: But, again, as the other suttas also say, in order to develop brahma-vihāras, you need to dwell like a brahma.

473
00:37:41,635 --> 00:37:59,039
[SPEAKER_00]: You need to be thoroughly withdrawn from all the unwholesome, so that this internal physicality and aspect and the sense bases, because the Buddha compared the sense bases as they're negative, they're like empty, empty village and so on, that you cannot possibly just put in front of you and see it like you would see sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches.

474
00:37:59,139 --> 00:38:01,100
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they're the utmost fundamental negative.

475
00:38:04,152 --> 00:38:07,035
[SPEAKER_00]: So, and then goes, yeah, those perceptions of impermanence.

476
00:38:07,115 --> 00:38:07,856
[SPEAKER_00]: I addressed that.

477
00:38:08,978 --> 00:38:12,462
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the point, sorry, maybe it was clear, but maybe I can just repeat.

478
00:38:13,523 --> 00:38:18,469
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, if we just read this sutta, the

479
00:38:20,721 --> 00:38:22,182
[SPEAKER_00]: Just the part about ānāpānasati.

480
00:38:23,362 --> 00:38:33,828
[SPEAKER_00]: And, eh... if... if you're able to just put everything else you heard about ānāpānasati aside, all the Burmese methods, all the energy manipulations, all the nostril watching, just... just forget about all of it.

481
00:38:34,388 --> 00:38:35,849
[SPEAKER_00]: Just read it on its own terms.

482
00:38:37,170 --> 00:38:40,571
[SPEAKER_00]: See what honestly would come up to your mind as... as what would I do?

483
00:38:41,972 --> 00:38:43,353
[SPEAKER_00]: How would I go about doing this?

484
00:38:45,250 --> 00:38:47,252
[SPEAKER_00]: And really try to understand it on that level.

485
00:38:48,193 --> 00:38:49,053
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's the point.

486
00:38:49,234 --> 00:38:55,819
[SPEAKER_00]: As I said, people fall into these expectations because they learned it... they learned about it through these techniques and methods and so on.

487
00:38:56,540 --> 00:38:59,783
[SPEAKER_00]: But just don't try and do ānāpānasati.

488
00:39:00,624 --> 00:39:01,244
[SPEAKER_00]: Sit down.

489
00:39:02,005 --> 00:39:03,226
[SPEAKER_00]: Recognize what's there.

490
00:39:03,466 --> 00:39:05,328
[SPEAKER_00]: As we said, recollect, breathe in, breathe out.

491
00:39:05,748 --> 00:39:06,509
[SPEAKER_00]: And stick with that.

492
00:39:07,230 --> 00:39:16,404
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that should be enough, by the way, to outline the entire domain of the internal, even more clearly, and certainly should be enough to

493
00:39:18,328 --> 00:39:20,710
[SPEAKER_00]: Remove all the patiga eventually.

494
00:39:20,790 --> 00:39:29,456
[SPEAKER_00]: That resistance, that aversion that you have towards aversion of your sense bases, that will also be abandoned.

495
00:39:29,956 --> 00:39:43,205
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you just even do that basic general practice of non-forgetfulness of breathing, you would be free from sensuality and ill-will.

496
00:39:44,526 --> 00:39:44,726
[SPEAKER_00]: So,

497
00:39:47,130 --> 00:40:02,055
[SPEAKER_00]: If you put everything you learned about it aside, as I said, like, you know, I can give you, oh, this is what ānāpānasati is about, but no, really, just sit down with it yourself and just just try not to forget about your breathing and see where it takes you.

498
00:40:03,175 --> 00:40:11,938
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it can kind of eventually sort of build up and paint a different picture of what ānāpānasati is actually about.

499
00:40:13,058 --> 00:40:16,299
[SPEAKER_00]: But obviously, as I said, if you're just doing it on top of your non-virtue, non-restraint,

500
00:40:17,387 --> 00:40:17,707
[SPEAKER_00]: Good luck.

501
00:40:17,787 --> 00:40:21,350
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, technically speaking, ānāpānasati sutta was taught to sotāpānas.

502
00:40:21,490 --> 00:40:26,394
[SPEAKER_00]: As a form of satipaṭṭhāna, it was a form that was taught to at least sotāpānas.

503
00:40:27,135 --> 00:40:30,137
[SPEAKER_00]: But, again, that's not to say you shouldn't be trying it.

504
00:40:30,197 --> 00:40:31,498
[SPEAKER_00]: But you should be trying to do it rightly.

505
00:40:31,778 --> 00:40:35,641
[SPEAKER_00]: Because in order to practice ānāpānasati, you need to be seeing your mind.

506
00:40:36,402 --> 00:40:39,644
[SPEAKER_00]: In order to see your mind, you need to have been discerning cittanimitta sufficiently.

507
00:40:39,664 --> 00:40:43,267
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's already a step away from sotāpāti.

508
00:40:44,492 --> 00:40:49,876
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you want to practice ānāpānasati, do it, but don't do it at the expense of the actual training.

509
00:40:52,197 --> 00:40:59,483
[SPEAKER_00]: Actual training in virtue, training in withdrawal, training in enduring things on the right level, and everything else, we talk about it on and on and on.

510
00:41:00,623 --> 00:41:11,491
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in the same sense, like, if we are withdrawn from, as I said, falling into the common expectations of what ānāpānasati is all about, and just read the sutta,

511
00:41:14,884 --> 00:41:16,086
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the purpose of it?

512
00:41:16,907 --> 00:41:20,151
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you could already see it's not a beginner's practice, obviously.

513
00:41:20,752 --> 00:41:29,282
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, the Buddha went through all this other stuff, and the elements, and maintaining this context, before, say, you know, you are equipped to practice ānāpānasati.

514
00:41:29,322 --> 00:41:32,806
[SPEAKER_00]: But, anyway, that doesn't mean you can't get the right idea of what it's about.

515
00:41:33,687 --> 00:41:49,163
[SPEAKER_00]: And you realize that since the whole point is to be developing that peripheral, the recognition of peripheral, the non-forgetfulness, means it's exactly, as I said, it's exactly the opposite of the common idea of concentration and absorption practices.

516
00:41:49,863 --> 00:41:54,428
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the main purpose of ānāpānasati is to unabsorb you from your senses.

517
00:41:55,928 --> 00:41:58,370
[SPEAKER_00]: By being unabsorbed, you get a full picture.

518
00:41:59,011 --> 00:42:05,678
[SPEAKER_00]: You get that negative of what those senses refer to, what the sense objects refer to, what the sense objects point to.

519
00:42:06,879 --> 00:42:11,263
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's how you start to outline the physicality, outline the feelings, outline the moods.

520
00:42:15,247 --> 00:42:20,392
[SPEAKER_00]: So, so yeah, you won't be able to just start practicing ānāpānasati rightly.

521
00:42:21,699 --> 00:42:33,942
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it's really a training of that, as we said, mindfulness, of that recollectedness that broadens the peripheral recognition without needing to directly attend to it.

522
00:42:34,443 --> 00:42:35,323
[SPEAKER_00]: But it doesn't mean you shouldn't.

523
00:42:35,363 --> 00:42:42,745
